      "claim": "L3 oral exposure records show measurable systemic exposure for related carbamate/benzylamine/anilide molecules (itopride AUC0-t ~12–13 µg·h/mL after 150 mg; bicalutamide Cmax ~1.6–2.2 µg/mL after 150 mg), consistent with oral absorption.",
      "card_ids": ["C82","C100","C96"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 solubility/dissolution analogs (benzocaine 1.68 mg/mL; mosapride >95% dissolution in 0.1 N HCl and high solubility in PEG400/glycerol formal/propylene glycol) support dissolution potential for an aniline/carbamate-like scaffold.",
      "card_ids": ["C142","C123","C115","C126","C151","C141","C148"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L5 efflux records for larger carbamate/aniline or peptidomimetic analogs (dabigatran etexilate efflux ratio 13.8 with intrinsic Papp 29×10^-6 cm/s; ximelagatran efflux ratio 34; EKB-569 efflux ratio >3) show P-gp efflux is possible for such scaffolds, but these are larger/more complex molecules and mechanism alone is not an F result; amlodipine, a smaller primary-amine/ester aryl-halide analog, shows no net efflux (ER ~0.96–1.14).",
      "card_ids": ["C158","C167","C198","C200","C203","C161"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "No query-specific direct F, permeability, or efflux measurement exists; unresolved uncertainty is expressed as moderate confidence and evidence gaps, not as a low prediction.",
      "card_ids": []
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "gut_wall_efflux_intestinal_metabolism",
      "applicability": "low",
      "direction": "contradictory",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C158","C167","C198"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query molecule.",
    "No query-specific Caco-2/PAMPA permeability or P-gp efflux assay; L5 analogs are indirect and mostly larger/more complex scaffolds.",
    "No intestinal or first-pass metabolism data for the carbamate/aniline/benzylamine motif.",
    "Reference contexts include cirrhosis and prandial conditions that may alter F; transferability to the query's condition is uncertain.",
    "Solubility of the query is not directly measured; logP suggests moderate solubility but may be limiting."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high: direct reference F values and L3 exposure support oral absorption, L4 solubility/dissolution analogs are supportive, and L5 provides only low-transferability mechanistic efflux evidence (with mixed no-efflux analogs) that is insufficient to affirm F < 20%. Confidence remains moderate because no query-specific F, permeability, or efflux data are available."
}

